# The Well — migration order and routing (ADR-101).
#
#   <database> <file> [notx] [superuser]
#                                apply <file> to <database>, in this order
#   skip <file>                  in this directory, deliberately never applied
#
# Read by db/init.sh (empty volume) and well-migrate (an existing Well);
# each records what it ran in that database's well_schema_migrations ledger.
# Cluster-level files (roles, databases, grants on databases) run against,
# and are recorded in, `postgres`. notx: statement by statement outside a
# transaction (CREATE DATABASE cannot run in one). Once 025 gives a
# database a non-superuser owner, its files run as that owner (SET ROLE),
# so what they create belongs to it; superuser: keep the superuser.
#
# Never edit a file once it is applied anywhere: the ledger holds its
# sha256 and well-migrate refuses to run past the difference. Add a new one.

